      "location": "docs/guides/operator/advanced-configuration.adoc:446-450"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "New exit-code contract lacks behavioral assertions",
      "description": "The new disabled-feature test checks only the error text, not the newly documented exit code `4`, and exercises only `metadata`, although `check` has a separate guard. Additionally, `testWrongVersions()` never asserts the incompatible-result exit code, which this change switches from `4` to `3`.\n\nBecause the compatibility guide explicitly directs automation to rely on exit codes rather than messages, these tests would miss regressions in the primary scripting contract. Assert exit code `4` for both disabled subcommands and exit code `3` for incompatible metadata.",
